# opus.ro + www.opus.ro — production.
#
# DO NOT install this file until the apex A record actually points at this box.
#
# Caddy tries to obtain a certificate for every hostname in its config as soon
# as the config loads. While opus.ro still resolves to GitHub Pages' IPs, those
# ACME challenges are answered by GitHub, not by this server, so every attempt
# fails. Beyond the log noise that burns Let's Encrypt's failed-validation rate
# limit, which can lock out issuance for the real cutover.
#
# Correct order (see deploy/README.md):
#   1. opus-common.caddy + opus-dev.caddy, verify dev.opus.ro over real HTTPS
#   2. repoint the apex at this box in IRD DNS
#   3. only then drop this file in and reload

opus.ro {
	root * /srv/opus/current
	import opus-site
}

www.opus.ro {
	redir https://opus.ro{uri} 308
}
